    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">GIC_PMEVFILTR&lt;n&gt;, n = 0 - 63</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">GIC PMU Event Filter Register</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>GIC PMU Event Filter Register</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_GICv5_EXT is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to GIC_PMEVFILTR&lt;n&gt; are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p><h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>GIC_PMEVFILTR&lt;n&gt; is a 64-bit register.</p>
      <p>This  register is part of the <a href="gic_pmu_frame.html">GIC_PMU_FRAME</a> block.</p><h2>Field descriptions</h2><h3>When GIC_PMEVTYPER&lt;n&gt;.PMEVTYPE IN {'01x'}:</h3><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>63</td><td>62</td><td>61</td><td>60</td><td>59</td><td>58</td><td>57</td><td>56</td><td>55</td><td>54</td><td>53</td><td>52</td><td>51</td><td>50</td><td>49</td><td>48</td><td>47</td><td>46</td><td>45</td><td>44</td><td>43</td><td>42</td><td>41</td><td>40</td><td>39</td><td>38</td><td>37</td><td>36</td><td>35</td><td>34</td><td>33</td><td>32</td></tr></thead><tfoot><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tfoot><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-63_48">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-47_32">EVENT_ID</a></td></tr><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="32"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">DEVICE_ID</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-63_48">Bits [63:48]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-47_32">EVENT_ID, bits [47:32]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>When filtering by EventID, the EventIDs that match this value are counted.</p>
<p>When GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_EID is 0, this field is IGNORED.</p>
<p>When GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_EID is 1, GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_EID_SPAN controls how the EventID is matched against this value.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_0">DEVICE_ID, bits [31:0]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>When filtering by DeviceID, the DeviceIDs that match this value are counted.</p>
<p>When GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_DID is 0, this field is IGNORED.</p>
<p>When GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_DID is 1, GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_DID_SPAN controls how the DeviceID is matched against this value.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h3>When GIC_PMEVTYPER&lt;n&gt;.PMEVTYPE IN {'00x'}:</h3><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_1"><thead><tr><td>63</td><td>62</td><td>61</td><td>60</td><td>59</td><td>58</td><td>57</td><td>56</td><td>55</td><td>54</td><td>53</td><td>52</td><td>51</td><td>50</td><td>49</td><td>48</td><td>47</td><td>46</td><td>45</td><td>44</td><td>43</td><td>42</td><td>41</td><td>40</td><td>39</td><td>38</td><td>37</td><td>36</td><td>35</td><td>34</td><td>33</td><td>32</td></tr></thead><tfoot><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tfoot><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_1-63_48">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_1-47_32-1">VM_ID</a></td></tr><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="3"><a href="#fieldset_1-31_29-1">TYPE</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="5"><a href="#fieldset_1-28_24">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="24"><a href="#fieldset_1-23_0-1">ID</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_1-63_48">Bits [63:48]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_1-47_32-1">VM_ID, bits [47:32] <span class="condition">when GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_VM_ID == '1'</span>:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>When filtering on VM_ID only events that are translated to virtual interrupt events matching this VM_ID are counted.</p>
<p>When an event is selected that does not support filtering on VM ID, this field is <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span> and has no impact on the counted events.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h4 id="fieldset_1-47_32-2"> <span class="condition">Otherwise</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_1-31_29-1">TYPE, bits [31:29] <span class="condition">when GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_INTID == '1'</span>:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Type of the interrupt.</p>
<p>When an event is selected that does not support filtering on INTID, this field is <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span> and has no impact on the counted events.</p><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>TYPE</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b010</td><td>
          <p>LPI</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b011</td><td>
          <p>SPI</p>
        </td></tr></table>
      <p>All other values are reserved.</p>
    <p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h4 id="fieldset_1-31_29-2"> <span class="condition">Otherwise</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_1-28_24">Bits [28:24]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_1-23_0-1">ID, bits [23:0] <span class="condition">when GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_INTID == '1'</span>:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>The ID of the interrupt.</p>
<p>ID and TYPE together form an INTID.</p>
<p>The monitored IRS may implement fewer than 24 bits of ID.  Unimplemented upper bits are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
<p>When GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_INTID is 1, GIC_PMEVFILT2R&lt;n&gt;.FILTER_INTID_SPAN controls how the INTID is matched against this value.</p>
<p>When an event is selected that does not support filtering on INTID, this field is <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span> and has no impact on the counted events.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h4 id="fieldset_1-23_0-2"> <span class="condition">Otherwise</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><div class="access_mechanisms"><h2>Access Instructions</h2><p>Accesses to this register use the following encodings:</p><div class="access_block"><p>Accessible at offset <span class="hexnumber">0xA00 + (8 * n)</span> from GIC_PMU_FRAME</p></div><ul><li>When PMROOTCR.RA is implemented, an access is Secure, and PMROOTCR.RA IN {'001', '000'}, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>When PMROOTCR.RA is implemented, an access is Realm, and PMROOTCR.RA IN {'010', '000'}, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>When PMROOTCR.RA is implemented, an access is Non-secure, and PMROOTCR.RA != '011', accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>When PMSCR.NSRA is implemented, (an access is Non-secure or an access is Realm), and PMSCR.NSRA == '0', accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>When Register is read-only, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RO</span>.
          </li><li>Otherwise, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
          </li></ul><p style="text-align: right">
